  "$comment": "Library surface materials, themes and tint swatches (map/materials.ts; maps, tiles, themes and Style Packs name a material or theme by `id`, so never rename or remove one). `materials` is MapMaker's palette order. A material is a procedural `pattern` (its painter is code: packages/client/src/materials/patterns.ts) in `base` and `accent` (#rrggbb), or a scanned `texture` set (content/textures.json: textures/<id>_color.jpg and _normal.jpg, _emission.jpg when `emissive`; `base` is its average colour, for minimaps and icons). `scale`: metres one repeat covers; `shine`: 0 matte to 1 glossy; `emissive`: glows whatever the light. A theme gives each surface slot (floor, walls, solids, underside, trim) its default `material` and optional `tint`, and the `sky` colour. No network code: materials and themes travel as their id inside the map. Edit, then run `node tools/content/materials.mjs`.",
